URL Shortener Service (Golang + Fiber + MongoDB + Redis)

This is a high-performance URL Shortener service built with Go Fiber, MongoDB, and Redis.
It allows users to submit long URLs, generate a unique short code, and redirect users efficiently.

Features
Feature	Description
Shorten URLs	Converts long URLs into short keys like http://localhost:8001/abc1234
Fast Lookup	Uses Redis Cache to speed up redirects (O(1) lookup)
Persistent Storage	Original mapping is saved in MongoDB
Automatic Redirect	Visiting the short URL redirects to the original URL
Scalable Architecture	Supports thousands of concurrent requests
Modular Code Structure	Clean architecture → handler, service, repository layers


shorten-service/
│── cmd/
│   └── main.go              # App entrypoint
│
│── internal/
│   ├── config/              # Env variables, app config
│   ├── db/
│   │   ├── mongo.go         # Mongo connection + collection init
│   │   └── redis.go         # Redis connection
│   ├── model/
│   │   └── url.go           # URL struct model
│   ├── repository/
│   │   └── url_repository.go# DB + Cache operations
│   ├── service/
│   │   └── url_service.go   # Business logic (generate short code etc.)
│   └── handler/
│       └── url_handler.go   # HTTP routes & request handling
│
├── go.mod
├── go.sum

Tech Stack

| Component     | Technology                 |
| ------------- | -------------------------- |
| **Language**  | Go (Golang)                |
| **Framework** | Fiber v2                   |
| **Database**  | MongoDB Atlas              |
| **Cache**     | Redis                      |
| **Runtime**   | Docker / Local development |
